Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env`.

```bash
# Environment (development | production). Controls cookie security.
NODE_ENV=development

# HTTP server
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=3000

# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins (no wildcard allowed).
# Production example: https://lifeos.app,https://www.lifeos.app
ALLOWED_ORIGINS="http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173"

# PostgreSQL connection string (managed DB recommended in production).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://lifeos:lifeos@localhost:5432/lifeos"

# JWT signing secret — use a long random value in production (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
JWT_SECRET=change-me

# Structured log level (trace | debug | info | warn | error).
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Rate limiting (global).
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=300
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=1 minute

# Stricter limits on auth endpoints.
LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=5
LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=1 minute
REGISTER_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10
REGISTER_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=1 minute
```
